          "decision": "approved-one-way",
          "reasonCode": "documented-sensitive-one-way",
          "reviewer": "endstate-maintainers",
          "reviewedOn": "2026-07-22",
          "evidence": "Authored module notes: Captures RealVNC Viewer preferences from HKCU\\Software\\RealVNC\\vncviewer (connection book entries, UI/display options, protocol tweaks). Saved per-connection passwords are documented in secrets and excluded from restore. HKCU-only capture; sensitivity medium because the connection book may reference internal hostnames. Confidence: medium — registry path confirmed from public RealVNC documentation and community reports. Authored secret warning: RealVNC Viewer stores per-connection saved passwords as encrypted registry values (Password / EncryptedPassword). The encryption is machine-bound; restoring these values on a different machine renders them unusable or, in some VNC implementations, silently insecure. Do not auto-restore saved credentials — reconnect and re-save passwords after a rebuild. Authored excluded secret or machine-bound paths: HKCU\\Software\\RealVNC\\vncviewer\\*\\Password, HKCU\\Software\\RealVNC\\vncviewer\\*\\EncryptedPassword"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
